    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "is Doug Burns with the Carol Times Herald and Iowa Political Mercury. We've talked today with Congressman Tim Ryan, Democratic candidate for president, have a particularly interesting discussion on his journey as a lifetime lifelong Catholic from his pro-life position to what is now a very strong pro-choice position on abortion. We go through a number of issues related to rural economic development. And then get into some pretty interesting conversations about our mutual background as guys in our in our forties in the fraternity system. Him at Bowling Green and me at Northwestern. So our fraternity is still relevant or are they? outdated and kind of a relic of a different era. That's something I've never talked to a presidential candidate about before. And then, near the end, we talk about his family life. He is at once a dad and a stepdad. He doesn't make that distinction. He has three kids, considers them all the same, but it is a blended family, so he does bring at age 45 that very American experience to the table as well. Anyway, interesting conversation. He represents the Youngstown area that has obviously had some struggles with modernity as manufacturing has departed our country. But he's fought to bring jobs back and he has some very good ideas on rural and economic development. So we're with him for about 40 minutes or so.",
