    "turn_text": "Yeah, I've been growing. I are very, very good friends. I would say this humbly as possible. I mean, I think, Kim and I have the most progressive economic agenda going when you're talking about really finding ways to get these industries that are growing and how do you get them into areas that have been disconnected, whether it's globalization, automation, deindustrialization, however you want to put it. plug these communities back in and the digital revolution and the modern day, the new industrial revolution that's happening around advanced manufacturing, 3D printing, additive manufacturing. Those jobs can't be done anywhere if you put the infrastructure in place, if you make sure that we have 5G everywhere in the country. If you make sure that the roads, the bridges, the downtowns. I mean, this is why people used to tease me when I first started on my first palm card.",
