    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "for the state senate, I had on there renovate the Robbins Theater. And it was an old theater, an old Warner Brothers Theater, and one of my smaller downtowns in Warren, Ohio. And it was like, you need the quality of life too. I mean, you're not going to get tech jobs in this area and keep young people and keep talent. If you don't also have the art community, vibrant music community, vibrant downtowns, vibrant bike trails, river walks, clean rivers. I mean, this has got to be part of a broader agenda. But I think what Rose doing and we've continued to do it. We did this. We did it. The first tour was started in the tour. I mean, Rose done one offs. The first tour was Youngstown, Ohio, Akron, Ohio. Then we went to Detroit and Flint, Michigan and then South Bend, Indiana. Then we did one in Charlotte and we went down to some rural areas in South Carolina. Went to Columbia and a couple other small towns and then Atlanta. And we just finished one this week where we did Columbus, Ohio, Youngstown and Pittsburgh. So we should talk about doing some kind of rural one, at least where there's a stop somewhere in rural Iowa. We had 13 in this last one, maybe 15 venture capitalists. And one of the person there was actually a business owner who, his business is how do you get companies to locate back office operations in communities outside of the big cities. This, I believe that in my agenda will have initiatives through the Department of Commerce that will help make this happen. I think you can have tax incentives, I think you can reward companies that do these kind of things, because if we don't have every community benefiting from it, then you know, what's the use? It's concentration. If you look at the communities that have them, they've got traffic problems. They've got all kinds of infrastructure issues that there's no affordable housing anywhere in town. If you're a working class person, you got to drive an hour and a half or take a bus an hour and a half into the town to work. So we're actually going to be relieving a lot of pressure in those areas too so it could really be a win-win across the board.",
