    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So you've been crisscrossing Iowa to a degree already, Congressman, when you drive from Carroll about an hour and a half to Des Moines, one thing that we noticed, those of us who do it with some frequency, is just the sprawl and growth, the sprawl and the suburbs. And 70% of Iowans are from Iowa. So when we see this growth ringing Des Moines or ringing Council of Omaha, it's sort of heartbreaking for somebody like me because I know that the people who are going to populate these, like, fast growing developments are going to be rural islands. What do we do to reverse that trend? Should I see that happening? Should I be excited that, like, one of my primary cities is becoming more vital, or should I be hurt and threatened by it?",
