    "turn_text": "I don't think so. I don't think so. Not in my opinion. Because the market's shifting so much. But here's the deal. We've got so many opportunities here. So electric vehicles, right? There's one to two million electric vehicles today. By 2030, there's going to be 30 million electric vehicles. Somebody's going to make those. Now, an FDR Democrat is going to say, how do we make those in the United States? How do we have an industrial policy in the United States, like Germany has, but frankly, like China has? Who's going to make these cars? Right now, China dominates 40 to 50% of the electric vehicle market. Same thing with solar. How do we make solar panels in the United States? Right now, China controls 60% of the solar panel market. Same with wind, same with artificial intelligence, same with additive manufacturing 3D printing. So when I'm president, I'm going to sit down with the venture capital community, sit down with the Department of Energy, Department of Transportation, probably Department of Defense, sit down with any emerging electric vehicle companies, the big three, we should sit down with and say, okay, forget Democrat Republican, how do we build electric vehicles in the United",
