    "turn_text": "proud of that rich tradition here in Carroll. There's a few walks away at St. Anthony Regional Hospital. We don't have a county hospital here, so that's been great for our tax situation because we have a non-profit that was started in 1905 by the Franciscan Sisters of Perpetual Adoration. People who live in this region also have a choice of two great K-12 systems. So, talk a little bit about how your Catholic faith, your private faith informs your public service. And then you've made a journey that on abortion, you know, from basically a pro-life position to pro-choice. What's interesting to me about that is, you know, the whole pro-choice movement is based on wanting to get converts. They sort of got you as a convert, now they don't trust you. So kind of unpack that multi-layered question there for me.",
