    "turn_text": "congresswoman out of Connecticut. And her and I hit it off because she's Italian and I'm Italian and I was new and I was 29 and we just became very good friends. We started having a conversation about reducing the need for abortion through contraception. And so we put this whole package together. Her and I, my goal was how do you get pro-life and pro-choice people together to reduce unintended pregnancies? And you do that primarily through prevention. Anyway, long story short. I built a relationship with Planned Parenthood and their leadership, Cecile Richards at the time, Nay Rall, and I started to meet women who had abortions. I'm a kid from just outside of Youngstown. I never talked to a woman who had an abortion, not that I knew of. And I started to meet these women who were in these very, very difficult circumstances, all of them different. And I started to really realize, like, I don't think, I became very uncomfortable with my position, my pro-life position. because I started to realize that I don't think that the government really has a role in all this. This is really",
